{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu09", "cards": [{"id": "u4.t.phytoplankton", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">phy<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">to<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">PLANK<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ton<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"phytoplankton\" data-audio=\"audio/phytoplankton.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: phytoplankton\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-phytoplankton.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Mixed phytoplankton under a microscope: diatoms and other tiny algae from the sea.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Mixed phytoplankton under a microscope: diatoms and other tiny algae from the sea.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的混合浮游植物：来自海洋的硅藻和其他微小藻类。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: University of Rhode Island/Stephanie Anderson · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"phytoplankton\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"62.275\" font-size=\"6.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Phytoplankton<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"62.625\" font-size=\"7.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Zooplankton<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Small<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">fish<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Plankton that make food by photosynthesis. They start most ocean food chains.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>浮游植物<\/b>：通过光合作用制造食物的浮游生物，是多数海洋食物链的起点。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">phyto = plant. Plant plankton.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">phyto = 植物。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Why are phytoplankton important?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">They make food and oxygen and begin ocean food chains.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.zooplankton", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">zoo<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">PLANK<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ton<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"zooplankton\" data-audio=\"audio/zooplankton.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: zooplankton\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-zooplankton.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" alt=\"A freshwater copepod, a common zooplankton animal, under a microscope (dark background). It is about 1 millimetre long.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A freshwater copepod, a common zooplankton animal, under a microscope (dark background). It is about 1 millimetre long.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下（暗背景）的淡水桡足类，一种常见的浮游动物，长约 1 毫米。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Janeklass · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY 4.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Freshwater_copepod_(Copepoda)_under_darkfield_microscopy.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"zooplankton\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"62.275\" font-size=\"6.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Phytoplankton<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"62.625\" font-size=\"7.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Zooplankton<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Small<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">fish<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Plankton that eat other organisms, including phytoplankton.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>浮游动物<\/b>：以其他生物（包括浮游植物）为食的浮游生物。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">zoo = animal. Animal plankton.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">zoo = 动物。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What do zooplankton eat?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Phytoplankton and other tiny organisms.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.diatom", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">DI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">a<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tom<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"diatom\" data-audio=\"audio/diatom.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: diatom\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-diatom.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"526\" alt=\"Diatoms under a microscope. Each one sits inside a glass-like shell.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Diatoms under a microscope. Each one sits inside a glass-like shell.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的硅藻。每一个都住在玻璃般的外壳里。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Prof. Gordon T. Taylor, Stony Brook University · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diatoms_through_the_microscope.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"diatom\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"28\" class=\"f6 k\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"60\" class=\"\"/><ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"36\" class=\"f6 k\"/><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"92\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">glass shell with two halves<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A single-celled alga with a glass-like shell made of silica.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>硅藻<\/b>：具有二氧化硅玻璃状外壳的单细胞藻类。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">dia = through, tom = cut: a shell in two halves.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">外壳分成两半。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What is a diatom&#x27;s shell made of?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Silica (glass-like).<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.dinoflagellate", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">di<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">no<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">FLAG<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">el<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">late<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"dinoflagellate\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: dinoflagellate\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-dinoflagellate.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Ceratium, a dinoflagellate, under a microscope. Its armour plates grow into long horns.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Ceratium, a dinoflagellate, under a microscope. Its armour plates grow into long horns.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下的角藻（一种甲藻）。它的甲板长成长长的角。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Keisotyo · <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ceratium_sp_umitunoobimusi.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"dinoflagellate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"32\" class=\"f5 k\"/><path d=\"M60 60 L140 60\" class=\"s\"/><path d=\"M72 40 Q85 58 80 80\" class=\"s\"/><path d=\"M130 40 Q116 58 120 80\" class=\"s\"/><path d=\"M62 60 Q40 40 30 55\" class=\"s\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">two flagella: spinning swimmer<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A single-celled alga with two flagella that spins as it swims. Some cause red tides.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>甲藻<\/b>：有两条鞭毛、边游边旋转的单细胞藻类，有些会引发赤潮。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">dino = whirling.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">dino = 旋转。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What do some dinoflagellates cause?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Red tides.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.algal-bloom", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term mid\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">AL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gal<\/span> <span class=\"st\">BLOOM<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"algal bloom\" data-audio=\"audio/algal-bloom.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: algal bloom\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-algal-bloom.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"640\" alt=\"An algal bloom in Lake Erie seen from a satellite. The milky green water is full of tiny algae.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">An algal bloom in Lake Erie seen from a satellite. The milky green water is full of tiny algae.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">卫星拍到的伊利湖藻华。乳绿色的湖水里满是微小的藻类。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Jesse Allen and Robert Simmon · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toxic_Algae_Bloom_in_Lake_Erie.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"algal bloom\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"52.95\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Nutrients<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"63.15\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">enter the<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"73.35\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">water<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Algae<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">multiply<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">fast<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"46.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Water<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">turns<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">green or<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"80.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">red<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A sudden, huge growth of algae in water.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>藻华<\/b>：水体中藻类突然大量繁殖。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">bloom = burst of growth, like flowers.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">bloom = 像开花一样突然繁盛。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What often starts an algal bloom?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Extra nutrients such as fertilizer in the water.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.red-tide", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">RED<\/span> <span class=\"st\">TIDE<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"red tide\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: red tide\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-red-tide.webp\" width=\"780\" height=\"548\" alt=\"A red tide off the coast of California. The water is coloured by billions of dinoflagellates.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A red tide off the coast of California. The water is coloured by billions of dinoflagellates.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">美国加州海岸的赤潮。海水被数以十亿计的甲藻染红。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: P. Alejandro Díaz · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La-Jolla-Red-Tide.780.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"red tide\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"54.575\" font-size=\"6.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Toxic<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"62.275\" font-size=\"6.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">dinoflagellates<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"69.975\" font-size=\"6.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bloom<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"58.05\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Shellfish<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"68.25\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">eat them<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"44.4\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">People who<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"53.6\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">eat the<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">shellfish<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">can get<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"81.2\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">sick<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">An algal bloom of toxic dinoflagellates that can poison shellfish and make people sick.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>赤潮<\/b>：有毒甲藻的藻华，可使贝类带毒、让人生病。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">red from the colour of the water.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水的颜色发红。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Why is it unsafe to eat shellfish during a red tide?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">They have eaten toxic algae and store the toxins.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u4.t.kelp", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">KELP<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"kelp\" data-audio=\"audio/kelp.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: kelp\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u4-kelp.webp\" width=\"240\" height=\"313\" alt=\"A kelp forest under water. Kelp is a large brown alga that can grow taller than a house.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A kelp forest under water. Kelp is a large brown alga that can grow taller than a house.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水下的海带森林。海带是一种大型褐藻，可以长得比房子还高。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Kip Evans · Public domain · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kelp_forest.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"kelp\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M40 100 Q30 70 45 50 Q55 30 40 12\" class=\"k s\"/><path d=\"M100 100 Q90 70 105 50 Q115 30 100 12\" class=\"k s\"/><path d=\"M160 100 Q150 70 165 50 Q175 30 160 12\" class=\"k s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"96\" width=\"180\" height=\"8\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f7\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">holdfast anchors it to rock<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A large brown alga that grows in cold sea water and forms underwater forests.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>海带（巨藻）<\/b>：生长在冷海水中的大型褐藻，能形成水下森林。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">kelp is multicellular but still a protist.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">海带是多细胞，但仍属原生生物。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Is kelp a plant?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. It is a multicellular protist (brown alga).<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u4.t.phytoplankton", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“Plankton that make food by photosynthesis. They start most ocean food chains.”<\/i>", "opts": ["vector", "nucleus", "organelle", "phytoplankton"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>phytoplankton<\/b>: Plankton that make food by photosynthesis. They start most ocean food chains. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">浮游植物<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.zooplankton", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“Plankton that eat other organisms, including phytoplankton.”<\/i>", "opts": ["eyespot", "phagocytosis", "amoeba", "zooplankton"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>zooplankton<\/b>: Plankton that eat other organisms, including phytoplankton. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">浮游动物<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.diatom", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A single-celled alga with a glass-like shell made of silica.”<\/i>", "opts": ["protist", "chlorophyll", "diatom", "mitochondrion"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>diatom<\/b>: A single-celled alga with a glass-like shell made of silica. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">硅藻<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.dinoflagellate", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A single-celled alga with two flagella that spins as it swims. Some cause red tides.”<\/i>", "opts": ["diatom", "food vacuole", "flagellate", "dinoflagellate"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>dinoflagellate<\/b>: A single-celled alga with two flagella that spins as it swims. Some cause red tides. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">甲藻<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.algal-bloom", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A sudden, huge growth of algae in water.”<\/i>", "opts": ["algal bloom", "photosynthesis", "vector", "cilia"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>algal bloom<\/b>: A sudden, huge growth of algae in water. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">藻华<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.red-tide", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“An algal bloom of toxic dinoflagellates that can poison shellfish and make people sick.”<\/i>", "opts": ["red tide", "zooplankton", "eyespot", "Plasmodium"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>red tide<\/b>: An algal bloom of toxic dinoflagellates that can poison shellfish and make people sick. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">赤潮<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u4.t.kelp", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A large brown alga that grows in cold sea water and forms underwater forests.”<\/i>", "opts": ["slime mold", "colonial organism", "kelp", "flagellate"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>kelp<\/b>: A large brown alga that grows in cold sea water and forms underwater forests. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">海带（巨藻）<\/span>", "whys": null}]}